-8c5f-accb98c18bb7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3e3c08003af3f6e400d705217e3d4d718feba88ed77a5cef4b2c69168a51710d","event_uuid":"26c533c3-eb27-45f7-89e0-baab5490312d","position":{"commit_sha":"4be3f26048c1251c35a34879debf38029092c7cd","position":"1788410168495559001-26c533c3-eb27-45f7-89e0-baab5490312d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff state. Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2531 (\"Derive the MCP model registry\"). Gate state at handoff: LLM-Review +1, Verified -1 — the code review PASSED and only CI is red.\n\nTwo failure signatures are open across this stack and neither root cause is confirmed yet:\n1. change 2530 fails the `require resolvable rebar ticket` job, although `rebar resolve` succeeds locally and the trailer is well-formed — the leading hypothesis is that the ticket is not visible to CI (the `tickets` branch may not have reached `origin`);\n2. pytest fails in ~50s on several changes, fast enough to be a collection/import error, and it does NOT reproduce locally.\n\nDo NOT close this ticket until its change is Verified +1 and merged. A subagent is driving the stack to green; a session-only cron loop (46e3b0eb) is harvesting reviews, landing green changes and closing merged tickets.\n\nNote for whoever lands this: amend only with `git commit --amend --no-edit`. Re-committing a change that already carries a Change-Id opens a DUPLICATE Gerrit change — that is how change 2534 came to exist and be abandoned.","timestamp":1788398745871066001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317556152213001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"282aa9e8-baa7-4db2-98a2-f638c34530cb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"818b8445-2886-4c02-a418-6ef6bfc72c0e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"785e-7221-5854-4dac"},{"link_uuid":"26c533c3-eb27-45f7-89e0-baab5490312d","provenance":"derived","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"8efe-9ceb-7d89-4a33"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F5 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), HIGH, ALREADY DRIFTED.\nDistinct from the MCP-tool-vs-facade parity gate (`8ce5-b870-601d-4715`): that one is\ntools-vs-facade, this one is models-vs-schemas. This is the PUBLISHED MCP wire contract.\n\n(The inventory cites `schemas/check_mcp_models.py`; the real path is\n`src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py`. Same file, prefix omitted.)\n\n## Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:1-24` declares itself a pydantic-only leaf with NO `rebar.*` import\nedges, so every canonical enum is hand-copied into it:\n\n- `:61-68` `PinStatus` (6 values) vs `llm/plan_review/pin_health.py:21`\n- `:54` `TargetPinStatus` (4) vs `pin_health.py:29` — and a THIRD copy as dict keys at `:193`\n- `:122` `FileImpactScope` vs `types.py:22`\n- `:284-295`, `:298`, `:336` vs `schemas/bridge_{run,status,access_check}.schema.json`\n\nThe drift gate that is supposed to catch this has two gaps, both verified:\n\n**1. It is enum-blind.** `missing_declarations` is exactly\n`sorted(set(schema_properties) - set(model_fields) - set(permissive))` — a property-NAME set\ndifference. The string `enum` does not appear anywhere in the module, so a model and its schema\ncan advertise different allowed VALUES for the same property and the gate is silent.\n\n**2. Its registry is hand-listed and 21 short.** `MODEL_SCHEMAS` registers 11 of the 32 public\n`*Out` models. Of the 21 unregistered, **9 have a schema file sitting right there** under the\nmodule's own `<snake_case>.schema.json` convention, so they could be checked today and are not:\n\n    ClaimResultOut, ClarityResultOut, CreateResultOut, DepsGraphOut, GateResultOut,\n    NextBatchOut, SearchResultOut, TicketStateOut, ValidateReportOut\n\n`TicketStateOut` is the largest surface in the file. Both `PlanReviewHealthAvailableOut` and\n`PlanReviewHealthUnavailableOut` — which carry the `PinStatus` copies — are absent entirely.\nThe remaining 12 unregistered models have no schema file and are correctly unregistered.\n\n## Approach — add-parity-check on values, and derive the registry\n\n1. **Enum parity.** Extend the check to compare each shared property's allowed VALUES, not only\n   its name, reporting the offending property and the two value sets.\n2. **Registry completeness.** Replace the hand-list with a derivation: every public `*Out` model\n   whose `<snake_case>` name has a schema file MUST be checked. A model with no schema file stays\n   out, and any deliberate exception is declared with a reason rather than omitted silently — the\n   defect here was omission-by-forgetting, which a derived registry makes impossible.\n\n**On epic AC2.** This does not merge distinct concepts: the models and the schemas already claim\nto describe the same wire payloads, and the module's docstring states the copies exist only to\nkeep it import-free. Nothing about the enum values is intended to differ. The 12 schema-less\nmodels are left alone precisely because they are NOT mirrors of anything.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: the gate compares enum VALUES for properties present on both sides, and fails when they\n      differ. Verified by a test seeding a model/schema pair whose value sets diverge and asserting\n      the failure names the property and both sets.\n- [x] AC2: the registry is derived, not hand-listed: every public `*Out` model with a matching\n      schema file is checked. Verified by a test asserting the derived set covers all 9 models\n      named above, which the current hand-list omits.\n- [x] AC3: a NEW `*Out` model with a schema file is picked up with no edit to the gate. Verified by\n      a test that synthesises such a pair and asserts it is included.\n- [x] AC4: a model with no schema file is excluded without error, and any deliberate exception\n      carries a stated reason. Verified by asserting the 12 schema-less models are absent and that\n      the exception list (if any) is non-empty only where a reason string is present.\n- [x] AC5: every drift the widened gate now finds is either FIXED or recorded as a declared,\n      reasoned exception — the gate must be green at rest, not merely more capable. Verified by the\n      gate passing on the committed tree.\n- [x] AC6: the enum copies that started this (`PinStatus`, `TargetPinStatus` incl. the third copy\n      at `:193`, `FileImpactScope`) are covered by AC1's comparison. Verified by naming them in the\n      test so a future refactor cannot quietly drop them from coverage.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py -q` — the\n  existing held-out suite plus the new enum-parity and registry-derivation cases (AC1-AC4, AC6).\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q` — proves the widened gate is green at rest (AC5); it runs\n  from a test rather than `make lint`, so this is where a regression would surface.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py","reason":"derive the registry, add enum-value comparison, and baseline the 41 pre-existing gaps against their own ticket"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py","reason":"the oracle: derivation, auto-pickup, enum comparison both ways, and green-at-rest"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","785e-7221-5854-4dac"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"42edfafb-6c13-4133-ba70-169eeedfecb0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"62eb-5e6f-512a-420d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP output models re-type canonical enums and the drift gate is enum-blind (mirror F5)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b163b14e-99f6-48dc-b2b6-a2ee1ece2a0b","8ae53bc3-3017-4991-af5e-9f5317de6482","47e5bc10-4811-449d-995f-f0753400cba6","d7251c90-3e9f-44be-9ce4-c0b0ca9fa690","a9a74ff5-1364-4897-b89a-44c9400e9713","818b8445-2886-4c02-a418-6ef6bfc72c0e","b974e254-01dc-4577-82ec-20dad2a910c4","14ecc37c-13bb-4cd2-9d65-5d93725bf3b4","42edfafb-6c13-4133-ba70-169eeedfecb0","5a1fc17d-cb00-45bd-8c5f-accb98c18bb7","26c533c3-eb27-45f7-89e0-baab5490312d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788416050854647001,"uuid":"35853f49-3c4a-435e-824d-2fb51350e8f4"}